      "final_text": "Done. `candidate/Solution.lean` compiles cleanly (`lake build Solution`, exit 0) with all 5 theorems proved and no `sorry`.\n\n**Fix:** `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)` \u2014 on loop exit (`z = y` twice in a row) it returns `min y z` instead of the raw last value. On raw `9999999998` the Babylonian iterates 2-cycle between `9999999998` and `9999999999`; the old code returned `9999999999` (rounds up), while the true root floors to `9999999998`. Verified by execution: `9999999998 \u2192 9999999998`, plus `9999999999 \u2192 9999999999`, `1 \u2192 100000`, `10^10 \u2192 10^10`, `0 \u2192 0`.\n\n**Proof outline:** a Nat mirror of the loop (`nstep`/`nseq`) with Newton bounds (`div_le_tval`, `step_upper`/`step_lower`, `step_succ`), seed `a/2 + 5\u00b710^9` shown in range, and a halving error bound vanishing after enough steps \u2014 so the Int `loop` provably stabilizes exactly at `Nat.sqrt (a\u00b710^10)` (`loop_corr`, `sqrt_pos_floor`). The three hard theorems then follow from `Nat.sqrt_le` / `Nat.lt_succ_sqrt` via `exact_mod_cast`.\n\n**Compliance:** only `candidate/Solution.lean` modified (stale scratch files from earlier probing removed; tree shows just that one file changed); imports limited to `VyperSqrt.Spec`, `VyperSqrt.Lemmas`, `Init.*`; no forbidden keywords (grep clean); theorem names/statements identical to `Challenge.lean`.",
